      spectral statistics, but could not hear the music or
      watch the intro run in real time.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the programme
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  01 HEADWATER     sunlit alpine dawn over a curved
                             concrete arch dam, three spillway
                             bays, mirror reservoir and Alps
      0:15  02 SLUICE        radial steel tainter gates lift;
                             aerated whitewater roars over the
                             ogee chute as the camera plunges
      0:30  03 SURGE HALL    an infinite subterranean concrete
                             cathedral; ceiling oculi pour
                             diagonal sunbeams onto flooded
                             turquoise mirror water
      0:52  04 PENSTOCK      freefall down a riveted vertical
                             steel intake shaft; strobe rings
                             shift from amber to electric cyan
      1:07  05 TURBINE       inside the scroll chamber: a
                             12-blade cast-bronze Francis
                             wheel, 24 glowing copper stator
                             coils and pulsing cavitation rings
      1:22  06 GRID          euphoric flight down an avenue of
                             ribbed porcelain insulators and
                             steel gantries as jagged plasma
                             arcs leap on every beat
      1:37  STILLWATER       blue-hour pull-back across the
                             calm upstream mirror lake; the
                             wall stencil reflects upside-down
                             under stars, crest lamps & greets

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows 10
      or 11, wait for "CLICK" (~6-8 seconds while the shaders
      compile and the soundtrack renders), then click to go
      fullscreen. No server, no browser flags. ESC exits
      fullscreen. A discrete GPU is expected. Tested on Edge
      with an RTX 5090 (1.2-1.7 ms/frame at 1080p).

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Five raymarched worlds live inside one signed-distance
      scene shader: the alpine arch dam & stepped spillway
      chute, the infinite G-Cans-style flooded surge hall
      (with domain-repetition cell-exit guards), the vertical
      steel penstock shaft, the helical bronze Francis
      turbine & stator chamber, and the porcelain insulator
      high-voltage switchyard with 3D jagged plasma arcs.

      Water surfaces cast a single-bounce mirror reflection
      using closed-form trigonometric ripple normals; one
      unified volumetric loop integrates sunbeams, spray mist,
      cavitation rings and plasma glow across all scenes. To
      keep ANGLE/D3D11 compilation fast (5-7 s instead of 70 s)
      without sacrificing visual richness, the shader limits
      map() to three call sites and prevents loop unrolling
      with a dynamic zero bound.

      The post shader combines a 12-tap Vogel-disc depth of
      field, 5-octave mipmap bloom, beat-synced exposure
      pulse, ACES filmic tone mapping, and Swiss typographic
      titles drawn from a shared 2D canvas atlas (also used
      as a painted stencil on the concrete dam wall).

      The soundtrack is rendered by a fragment shader into a
      4096x1456 RGBA32F texture at 48 kHz (124.24 s). RG holds
      the dry stereo mix (punchy kick, rolling 16th bass,
      snare, hats, FM bell arpeggio, detuned saw pad, bit-
      packed 32-step D-minor/Dorian anthem lead and risers);
      BA feeds a 4-line Householder FDN concrete-hall reverb
      and soft bus compressor in JavaScript so percussion
      stays tight while melodies ring in the hall.

